---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About | plansplease"
  description="plansplease gives the useful pages made by coding agents a place to land."
  activePath="about"
>
  <section class="prose-page" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <h1 id="about-title">A place for the useful things agents make.</h1>
    <p>
      plansplease is a small open-source project for turning agent-made HTML into something you can
      open again.
    </p>

    <ul class="prose-list">
      <li>
        <h2>It starts on your machine</h2>
        <p>
          The CLI gives a standalone HTML file or page folder a local URL. Use it while the agent is
          still working and keep your project setup untouched.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>The cloud keeps the useful copy</h2>
        <p>
          The managed workspace accepts one standalone HTML file at a time. It is private to your
          account in the current alpha.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Small is a product decision</h2>
        <p>
          A page does not need a full application, a deployment pipeline, or a new project before it
          can be useful. Start with the artifact in front of you.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Built in the open</h2>
        <p>
          The source is available on <a href="https://github.com/abijith-suresh/planview">GitHub</a>.
          Self-hosting and richer uploads are part of the work ahead, not promises of the current
          alpha.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
